@startuml
' Figure 4.3 – System sequence diagram: sign in and silent token refresh
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram Sign in
autonumber "0 :"

participant "User" as U
participant "Browser\napplication" as W
participant "System" as A
participant "Database" as D

U -> W : Submit email and password
activate W
W -> A : POST /auth/login
activate A
A -> D : Read the account by email
activate D
D --> A : Account row
deactivate D
A -> A : Compare the password against the bcrypt hash

alt credentials invalid, or the account is banned
  A --> W : 401, generic message
  W --> U : Display "invalid credentials"
else credentials valid
  A -> A : Issue an access token (15 min)\nand a refresh token (7 days)
  A --> W : Tokens and the account profile
  W -> W : Store the access token and set the auth cookie
  W --> U : Redirect to the feed
end
deactivate A
deactivate W

|||

group Silent refresh, on any later request
  W -> A : GET a protected resource
  activate A
  A --> W : 401, the access token has expired
  W -> A : POST /auth/refresh with the refresh token
  A -> A : Rotate the refresh token and issue a new access token
  A --> W : New tokens
  W -> W : Refresh the auth cookie as well as the store
  W -> A : Retry the original request
  A --> W : 200
  deactivate A
end

note over U, D
  The cookie is refreshed as well as the client store. Before
  Phase Q it was written only at sign-in, so every session died
  silently after 15 minutes and unsaved editor work was lost.
end note
@enduml
